nue in its current status that  party that she's a member of is loosely  associated with the Democratic Party on  the mainland but she herself is not a  full-blown Democrat the criticism she's  been expressing quite publicly from the  capital is similar to what we've been  hearing from small town mayors across  the island there's frustration that the  central government they're led by the  governor isn't necessarily being  responsive when I talked to him  yesterday I asked him about this I said  we're hearing from a lot of the mayor's  who are frustrated about this he says  look I understand it's their job to be  worried about their constituents we're  doing what we can to get supplies into  their hands to make sure that the  situation in their towns is being  addressed and he said in the coming days  as these as he kept saying boots on the  ground arrived to provide assistance the  situation should have  proved dramatically will see we will ed  O'Keefe in our Washington bureau this  morning and thank you
 

